    "review": {
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "base_commit": "5baa70b2f3d57c9bab9fe0163197c5614fe2657f",
      "scope": "Reviewed frozen working-tree bytes after the throughput/reliability revision. The base commit is the comparison baseline, not the modified runtime. Hashes are review tripwires, not a Rust/SQLite/Redis/filesystem refinement proof.",
      "correspondence": [
        "NonceAllocator now models consumed-count floor with out-of-order retained receipt cleanup; separate bounded-page/RPC concurrency tests cover scheduling, not model throughput or fairness.",
        "EOA Uncertain retains exact borrowed wire on all dispatch errors; same-identity retry stutters in EoaRecovery, included receipt only restores submitted projection. NOOP reserves submitted hash before dispatch; automatic NOOP reconciliation is not modeled or implemented.",
        "DisasterRecovery terminal attribution requires the same admission independently executed its recorded attempt. Actual hash/signature/UserOperation computation and endpoint/genesis validation remain implementation checks.",
        "Exact attempt and unchanged checkpoint no-ops retain health/owner/CAS guards; admission overload makes no durable transition. Retained terminal retries do not enqueue new work.",
        "Solana independent signature reservation precedes Redis attempt storage; missing projection after SQL commit parks. The Redis and authority models are separate and not mechanically composed.",
        "Bundled EIP-7702 is disabled and legacy work parks; no dedicated protocol qualification is claimed. Streaming export, HTTP authentication/semaphores and provider genesis checks are outside the state-machine proof."
      ],
      "test_fixture_followup": {
        "date": "2026-09-26",
        "path": "executors/src/eoa/store/tests.rs",
        "reason": "Linux CI stalled at the retained-backlog fixture after its predecessor passed. Replace one 100k-command setup pipeline with 1,000-command batches, each with 10s timeout, and assert exact production-cap cardinality before unchanged cap/cap-minus-one budget assertions. No production or model semantics changed; observed buffering pressure is a diagnosis to verify on Linux, not an established Redis library defect."
      },
      "progress_scheduling_followup": {
        "date": "2026-09-26",
        "paths": [
          "executors/src/eoa/worker/mod.rs",
          "executors/src/eoa/worker/scheduling_tests.rs"
        ],
        "reason": "Reviewed successful-cycle result construction: sent counts only moved-to-submitted acknowledgments, recovered counts submitted-projection reconciliation/acknowledgment, while uncertain attempts retain borrowed state. Only positive nondelegation plus unsigned backlog plus either positive progress counter skips delay and still rejoins queue tail. Delegated/unknown/no-progress/finality-only/error handling retain existing delays. EoaRecovery already admits transitions without wall-clock waits; QueueLease keeps fenced completion and pending membership. Timing, fairness, mixed-progress unknown-retry RPC costs and throughput remain outside these finite safety models. Real Redis regression exercises actual queue lease completion, tail ordering, ready work and rounded delayed scores."
      }
    }
  },
